# Assignment 3 – Terminal Navigation Practice

## Objective
To practice basic terminal commands using PowerShell.

## Commands Practiced

1. `pwd` – Show the current folder.
2. `mkdir website` – Create a folder.
3. `cd website` – Enter the folder.
4. `mkdir css` – Create the CSS folder.
5. `mkdir images` – Create the images folder.
6. `ni index.html` – Create an HTML file.
7. `ni css/style.css` – Create a CSS file.
8. `cd css` – Enter the CSS folder.
9. `cd ..` – Return to the parent folder.
10. `ls -Recurse` – List files and folders.
11. `Rename-Item index.html home.html` – Rename the file.
12. `Rename-Item home.html index.html` – Rename it back.
13. `code .` – Open the folder in VS Code.

## Result
I practiced creating folders and files, navigating directories, listing files, and renaming files using PowerShell.
